zΔ⚡b|-1|+{{A|=1|+out%7Ca specific file compa|=1|+ison utility%7Cfile|=1|-2|+comparison in general%7CFile comparison%7Cdiffs in Wikipedia%7C:help:diff%7Cother uses%7CDIFF (disambiguation){{!}}DIFF}}%0A{{lowercase%7Ctitle%3Ddiff}}|=19|+e %3D diff%0A%7C titl|=38|+caption %3D %0A%7C |=15|+screenshot alt %3D %0A%7C collapsible %3D %0A%7C |=9|-1|+[[|=f|-1|+]]%0A%7C developer %3D [[AT&T Bell Laboratories]]%0A%7C released %3D {{Start date and age%7C1974%7C6}}%0A%7C latest release version %3D |=4e|+%7C programming language %3D %0A%7C platform %3D [[Unix]] and [[Unix%2Dlike]]%0A%7C genre %3D [[Command (computing)%7CCommand]]%0A%7C license %3D %0A%7C website %3D %0A%7C standard %3D %0A%7C AsOf %3D %0A|=6|+[[|=9|+]]|=27|+[[|=f|+]]|=4d|+[[|=d|+]]|=70|+[[|=14|+]]|=1c7|+[[|=b|+]]|=2|+<ref>MacKenzie ''et al.''  "Binary Files and Forcing Text Comparison" in ''Comparing and Merging Files with GNU Diff and Patch''.  Downloaded 28 April 2007.  [https://www.gnu.org/software/diffutils/manual/html_node/Binary.html]</ref>|=25|+[[patch (computing)%7C|=5|+]]|=2b|+[[Unix]]|=9|+[[patch (Unix)%7C{{Mono%7Cpatch}}]]|=66|+[[|=4|+]]|=87|+<ref>Eric S. Raymond (ed.), [http://catb.org/jargon/html/D/diff.html|=1|+&ldquo;diff&rdquo;], ''|=4|+Jargon File'', version 4.4.7</ref> The [[POSIX]]|=5c|+<ref>{{cite book%7Cauthor1 %3D IEEE Computer Society%7Cauthor2%2Dlink %3D The Open Group%7Cauthor2 %3D The Open Group%7Cdate%3D26 September 2008%7Ctitle %3D Standard for Information Technology&mdash;Portable Operating System Interface (POSIX) Base Specifications, Issue 7%7Cpages %3D 2599–2607%7Cauthor1%2Dlink %3D IEEE Computer Society}} IEEE Std. 1003.1%2D2001 specifies traditional, "ed script", and context diff output formats; IEEE Std. 1003.1%2D2008 added the (by then more common) unified format.</ref>|=6bf7|
