# 000900-000999/20200428T015711Z_953597981.wiki
zΔ⚡b|=618b|+[[Vim (text editor)%7CVim]] provides '''vimdiff''' to compare two, three or four files, with differences highlighted in color.<ref>{{Cite web%7Curl%3Dhttp://vimdoc.sourceforge.net/htmldoc/diff.html#vimdiff%7Ctitle%3DVim documentation: diff%7Cwebsite%3Dvimdoc.sourceforge.net%7Caccess%2Ddate%3D28 April 2020%7Cquote%3DThe easiest way to start editing in diff mode is with the "vimdiff" command. This starts Vim as usual, and additionally sets up for viewing the differences between the arguments. <br />'''vimdiff file1 file2 [file3 [file4]]'''<br /> This is equivalent to:<br />'''vim %2Dd file1 file2 [file3 [file4]]'''<br />}}</ref>%0A%0A|=160d|
