zΔ⚡b|=618b|-262|=160d|
# 000900-000999/20200502T033415Z_954384124.wiki
zΔ⚡b|=618b|+[[Vim (text editor)%7CVim]] provides '''vimdiff''' to compare from two to eight files, with differences highlighted in color.<ref>{{Cite web%7Cauthor%2Dlink%3DBram Moolenaar%7Cfirst%3DBram%7Clast%3DMoolenaar%7Curl%3Dhttps://vimhelp.org/diff.txt.html#vimdiff%7Ctitle%3DVim documentation: diff%7Cwebsite%3Dvimdoc.sourceforge.net%7Caccess%2Ddate%3D1 May 2020%7Cquote%3DThe easiest way to start editing in diff mode is with the "vimdiff" command. This starts Vim as usual, and additionally sets up for viewing the differences between the arguments. <br />'''vimdiff file1 file2 [file3] [file4] [...file8]'''<br /> This is equivalent to:<br />'''vim %2Dd file1 file2 [file3] [file4] [...file8]'''<br />}}</ref>%0AWhile historically invoking the diff program, modern vim uses the xdiff library code, providing improved speed and functionality.<ref name%3D"brabandt2018>{{Cite web%7Ctitle%3DThe power of diff%7Curl%3Dhttps://vimways.org/2018/the%2Dpower%2Dof%2Ddiff/%7Cdate%3D1 December 2018%7Cwebsite%3DVimways%7Caccess%2Ddate%3D1 May 2020%7Cfirst%3DChristian %7Clast%3DBrabandt%7Curl%2Dstatus%3Dlive%7Carchive%2Durl%3Dhttps://web.archive.org/web/20181202020105/https://vimways.org/2018/the%2Dpower%2Dof%2Ddiff/%7Carchive%2Ddate%3D2 December 2018}}</ref> A selection of diff algorithms be can specified including myers, patience, histograms, or minimal.<ref>{{Cite web%7Ctitle%3DVim: options.txt diffopt%7C%7Cauthor%2Dlink%3DBram Moolenaar%7Cfirst%3DBram%7Clast%3DMoolenaar%7Curl%3Dhttps://vimhelp.org/options.txt.html#%2527diffopt%2527%7Cwebsite%3Dvimhelp.org%7Caccess%2Ddate%3D1 May 2020}}</ref>%0A%0A|=160d|
