# 000900-000999/20200627T182259Z_964807739.wiki
zΔ⚡b|=2f72|-94|+O|=6|-84|=2|-a|+v|=1|-28|=2|-9|=1|-16|=1|-1|=1|-10|=2|-12|=2|-18|=1|-34|=1|-46|=1|-18|=1|-a|=1|-7|=1|-9|=1|-b1|=2|-6|=1|-9a|=1|-12|=1|-1b1|=28a5|+ Implementations and related programs{{anchor%7COthers}} |=1|+%3D%0AChanges since 1975 include improvements to the core algorithm, the addition of useful features to the command, and the design of new output formats. The basic algorithm is described in the papers ''An|=2|+(ND) Difference Algori|=2|+m and its Variations'' by Eugene W. My|=3|+<ref>{{cite journal%7Cauthor%3DE. Myers%7Ctitle%3DAn O(ND) Difference Algorithm and Its Variations%7Cjournal%3DAlgorithmica%7Cvolume%3D1%7Cissue%3D2%7Cyear%3D1986%7Cpages%3D251–266%7Cdoi%3D10.1007/BF01840446%7Cciteseerx%3D10.1.1.4.6927}}</ref> and in ''A File Comparison Program'' by Webb Miller and Myers.<ref>{{cite journal%7Cauthor1%3DWebb Miller %7Cauthor2%3DEugene W. Myers %7Ctitle%3DA File Comparison Program%7Cjournal%3DSoftware — Practice and Experience%7Cvolume%3D15%7Cissue%3D11%7Cyear%3D1985%7Cpages%3D1025–1040%7Cdoi%3D10.1002/spe.4380151102%7Cciteseerx%3D10.1.1.189.70 }}</ref> The algorithm was independently discovered and described in ''Algorithms for Approximate String Matching'', by [[Esko Ukkonen]].<ref>{{cite journal%7Cauthor%3DEsko Ukkonen%7Ctitle%3DAlgorithms for Approximate String Matching%7Cvolume%3D64%7Cjournal%3DInformation and Control%7Cissue%3D1–3%7Cyear%3D1985%7Cpages%3D100–118 %7C doi %3D 10.1016/S0019%2D9958(85)80046%2D2%7Cdoi%2Daccess%3Dfree}}</ref> The first editions of the diff program were designed for line comparisons of text files expecting the [[newline]] character to delimit lines. By the 1980s, support for binary files resulted in a shift in the application's design and implementation.%0A%0AGNU diff and diff3 are included in the '''diffutils''' package with other diff and [[Patch (Unix)%7Cpatch]] related utilities.%0ANowadays there is also a '''patchutils''' package that can combine, rearrange, compare and fix context diffs and unified diffs.%0A%0A%3D%3D%3D Formatters and front%2Dends|=128|+ by reconciling two diffs|=c0|+ for [[merge (revision control)%7Cmerging]].|=3d|-2a|=2|-7d|=a5|-80|=74d|+%3D%3D%3D Algorithmic derivatives %3D%3D%3D%0A|=3e4|-8|+ I|=1|-3|=1|-3|+addi|=2|+o|=1|-1|+,|=1|-3|+f|=2|+e |=1|+ools |=1|+hat perform s|=1|+ntax%2Daware|=1|-1|+d|=4|-1|+include:%0A*|=1|-1|+C%2B%2B: z|=1|+gras|=1|-2|+op|=1|-2|+, AST%2Db|=1|+sed.<ref>{{cite web %7C|=2|+tle%3Dxaizek/z|=1|-4|+grascope|=1|+%7Curl%3D|=4|+s|=3|-4|+gi|=1|-5|+hub|=5|-8|+x|=1|-1|=1|-7|+zek|=1|+zog|=1|+ascop|=1|-2|=1|-4|+%7Cweb|=1|-1|+it|=1|-1|+%3DG|=1|-1|=1|+Hub|=1|+%7Cda|=1|-1|+e%3D26|=1|-4|+M|=1|+y 2020}}</|=2|+f>%0A*|=5|+:|=1|+Daisydiff,|=3f|-2|+html%2D|=1|-3|+iff|=1|-4|=1|+.%0A*|=4|+:|=1|-d|+''xm|=1|+d|=1|-1|+ffpatc|=1|-2|+''|=11|+ ''xmldiffmerge'' for|=a4|-15|+*|=3|-3|+JavaScri|=1|-1|=1|-2|+]]:|=1|-1|+ast|=1|-4|=1|-4|+ (AST%2Dba|=1|-1|+ed).%0A*|=1|+Mu|=1|-2|+t|=1|-1|+%2Dl|=1|-2|=1|-6|+guag|=1|+: [[P|=1|-2|+etty|=1|-1|+D|=3|-7|+]]|=1|-5|+(forma|=1|-2|=1|-3|+cod|=3|-2|+n|=1|-3|=1|-2|=1|-7|+he|=1|-1|=5|-1|+)<|=2|-2|+f>Ch|=1|-3|=1|-3|+ey,|=1|-4|+Aus|=3|-1|+.|=1|-4|+''Pre|=1|-8|=1|-4|+y|=1|-1|+D|=1|-9|=3|-a|+%2D|=1|-2|+Docu|=2|-4|=2|-1|=1|-9|+t|=1|-2|+on''.|=1|-8|=4|-1|=3|-2|+pre|=1|-3|+tydiff|=7|-2|=1|-7|+u|=1|-b|=1|-10|=2|-1|=1|-6|=1|-1|+i|=1|-19|+n.php|=6|-8|+%0A%0A'''sp|=1|-2|+ff'''|=1|-c|+i|=1|-5|+ |=1|-3|+ |=1|-b|=1|-21|+ri|=1|-1|+n|=1|-1|+ |=1|-6|+f ''|=1|-3|=1|-5|+ff'' |=1|+h|=1|-2|+t ign|=1|-2|=1|-8|=2|-1|+ |=1|-14|+i|=1|-4|=1|-4|=1|-14|=1|-11|+e|=1|-1|=1|-14|=1|-3|=1|-1|+ |=1|+n |=1|-a|=1|-9|=1|-1|+a|=5|-1|+poi|=1|-1|+t|=1|-2|=1|-7|+a|=1|-1|=1|+ul|=5|-7|=1|-8|=1|-5|+wi|=1|-4|=1|-2|+ |=1|-17|+oun|=1|-2|+off |=1|-f|+r|=1|-5|+ors|=27|-4|+,|=1|-7|+b|=1|-1|=1|-c|+h o|=2|-e|=38|-2a|=c5|+ spiff outputs to the [[standard output]] in standard diff format and accepts inputs in the [[C (programming language)%7CC]], [[Bourne shell]], [[Fortran]], [[Modula%2D2]] and [[Lisp (programming language)%7CLisp]] [[programming language]]s.|=14e|-5|+<re|=2|+name%3D"d|=1|-1|+n|=1|-2|+callme">{{ci|=1|-1|+e|=1|+web%7Curl%3Dh|=1|-2|=1|-5|+p|=1|+://gi|=1|-2|+hub.com/|=1|+ontc|=1|-1|+llme|=1|-1|=1|-1|+m/spiff%7C|=1|+itle%3Ds|=1|+iff%7Ca|=2|-4|+hor%3Ddo|=1|-2|=1|+c|=1|-1|+llmedotcom%7Caccess|=2|+te%3D2013%2D06%2D16}}</|=1|-4|+e|=1|+><re|=1|+>{{cite|=1|-1|+web%7Curl%3Dhttps://stack|=1|+ve|=1|+flow.co|=1|+/a/1489107/2291035%7Cd|=2|-1|+e%3D2009%2D09%2D28%7C|=1|-1|+uthor%3DDavi|=1|-1|+e%7Ctitle%3Dstackoverflow%7C|=4|-1|+ssda|=1|-1|+e%3D2013%2D06%2D16}}</ref><ref|=1|-1|=1|+ame%3D"h|=2|+x">{{ci|=1|-1|+e|=1|-1|+web%7Curl%3Dhttp://hpux.co|=1|-1|+nec|=1|+.org.uk/hppd/|=1|+pux/T|=1|-6|+xt/s|=1|-1|+iff%2D1.0/%7Ctitle%3DHP%2DUX P|=1|-1|=1|-3|+t|=4|-1|=2|-3|+d Archivin|=1|-2|=1|-8|+l|=1|-1|+cation%3DUK%7Cfi|=1|+st%3DDa|=1|+i|=1|+l|=1|+W%7Cla|=1|+t%3DNac|=1|+bar%7Cdat|=1|-5|+%3D1999%2D12%2D01%7Caccessdate%3D2013%2D06%2D13}}</ref>%0A%0AThe|=3|-2|+git]] ve|=1|+sion con|=2|+ol progr|=1|-4|+m|=1|-3|+pr|=1|+vi|=1|+es fo|=1|-6|+r|=1|-2|=1|+iff|=1|-3|+algor|=1|+thm|=1|-1|+ to choose|=1|-2|+f|=2|-3|=1|-2|+. O|=1|-1|+e|=1|+a|=1|-2|=1|-1|+orithm c|=1|-1|+ll|=1|-3|+d "h|=2|-8|+t|=5|-1|+" |=1|+s ge|=1|+erally re|=1|+arded|=1|-1|=1|-2|+s m|=1|+ch better th|=1|+n the ori|=1|+inal "My|=1|-2|+r|=1|+" algorithm|=1|-5|+<|=2|-2|=1|+>{{c|=1|-1|+t|=2|-4|+web %7Cl|=1|+st1%3DNug|=1|+oho %7Cf|=1|+r|=1|-2|+t1%3DYusuf|=1|+Sulis|=1|+y|=1|-1|+ %7C|=1|+a|=1|+t2|=1|+Hata %7Cfirst2|=1|-7|+Hid|=1|-1|+ak|=1|-8|+ %7Clast3%3DMatsu|=1|-1|+oto|=1|-2|+%7Cfirst3%3DKe|=2|-3|=1|-9|+hi %7Ctitle%3DH|=1|-9|+w d|=3|-2|+er|=1|-1|+n|=1|-6|+ are |=4|-c|+e|=2|-6|+n|=1|-1|+ |=4|-7|+ algorithms |=2|-4|+ Git?: Us|=1|-2|=1|-2|+%2D%2Dh|=1|-3|=1|+t|=1|+gram |=1|-1|+or|=1|-3|+co|=1|-1|+e changes %7Curl%3D10.1007/s10664%2D019%2D09772%2Dz %7C|=1|+eb|=1|-5|+ite%3DE|=1|-1|+pirica|=1|-1|=1|-2|+S|=7|-1|+ Engineering |=1|-1|+pag|=1|+s%3D790–823 %7C|=1|-9|+anguag|=1|-3|+%3Den|=1|-1|+%7Cdo|=1|-8|+%3D10.1007/|=1|-4|+10664%2D019%2D09772%2Dz|=1|-6|=1|-d|+dat|=1|+%3DJa|=1|-1|+uary 2020|=2|+</ref>|=